#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:5
#: 93f208faadce41908d9577b0495e44a6
msgid "Setting up the Build Environment on Windows 10 using WSL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:7
#: a0bb6a7632c64a0d8cd377684e921831
msgid "These setup instructions describe how to set up \"Windows Subsystem for Linux\" which allows building with waf."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:12
#: c57ce3b9627c49d393915e9f2f3fb40d
msgid "It involves enabling the built-in Windows Linux environment (WSL) in Windows, installing a compatible Linux distribution, and finally installing the ArduPilot build environment as if it were a normal Linux system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:14
#: 18b8a4c630ad4dd7a6b82e2d1a152920
msgid "Upon completion, you will be able to build ArduPilot binaries and run the native ArduPilot SITL simulator, including the MAVProxy developer Ground Control Station. You will also be able to use the majority of Linux development features such as debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:18
#: 3a6b88e7268f420f8e7f06344f9fefcb
msgid "WSL Setup Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:19
#: a489e938c4624875a25ee659347c349b
msgid "The official instructions are `here <https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install-win10>`_ but the steps are also listed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:21
#: 8fedf9dcf2dc45db94db43431c248308
msgid "Enable WSL by opening \"Control Panel\", \"Programs\", \"Turn Windows features on or off\", selecting \"Windows Subsystem for Linux\", and press OK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:26
#: d3c85e8c11af4bf288df168143f48df8
msgid "From a web browser open `https://aka.ms/wslstore <https://aka.ms/wslstore>`_ which should open the Microsoft store to allow installing Ubuntu. Then Launch Ubuntu and fill in a username and login"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:31
#: 1542267e96cf4a5ab92579d0ebc61367
msgid "From the Start menu, start the \"Ubuntu\" application and then follow the :ref:`Ubuntu instructions to install ArduPilot development environment <building-setup-linux>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:35
#: 0cead283517f4969b313ebff63140d46
msgid "Compilation speeds will be much faster if the ArduPilot repository is downloaded inside of WSL's file system and not externally in the normal Windows file structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:37
#: ba4d9c2fab8c4f0e8d41eb15a4d9c747
msgid "To reload the path variables in WSL either close the terminal and reopen it or use: ``logout``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:39
#: c3557974984a41f688566a0e533d1643
msgid "If using Windows 10 install an XWindows application to run graphical programs such as SITL by installing `VcXsrv <https://sourceforge.net/projects/vcxsrv/>`_, `Cygwin X <https://x.cygwin.com/>`_ or `Xming <https://sourceforge.net/projects/xming/>`_ on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:41
#: 248a67786ed44e388a356b758fdb5601
msgid "If desired, change default WSL parameters as described `at this link <https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/wsl-config#configure-global-options-with-wslconfig>`_. These parameters allow you to set for example the amount of memory and number of processors used by WSL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:45
#: d4c8ef30dd9b487d9d84eeb7e19c9848
msgid "It is recommended to set memory limits as WSL2 currently does not release memory back to Windows properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:47
#: 8fc7a90ef11c4801b42904ea4c0a9d9b
msgid "Create or edit the file at the following location according to your needs and system specifications, ``C:\\Users\\<yourUserName>\\.wslconfig``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:58
#: c032dfd478c14d32b9176ea04faf38ea
msgid "WSL1 vs WSL2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:59
#: db2a225054d04a6aa5de36f54b5db600
msgid "WSL2 is the latest version of the Windows10 Subsystem for Linux. It is many times faster than WSL1 and is therefore preferred for building the code in terms of compilation speed. It can also run MAVProxy and native SITL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:63
#: d34c9a5381df4dd2bd9beafe8fa20d7d
msgid "Uploading to a board using WSL2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:65
#: cfd588c0b5394052ba6f982d88254636
msgid "Uploading to boards (e.g. ``./waf plane --upload``) in WSL2 is possible; however, an installation of Python must exist on the Windows side. Install these packages in Windows Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:71
#: f81aa3e644cd42d9826c544595471e7e
msgid "As of July 2022, Microsoft's solution of providing USB access to WSL2 via usbipd does not work for accessing the bootloader on the device due to slow mounting times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:73
#: 72039f91bd63440a9c5906dbed936506
msgid "WSL1 can upload to boards by default with no additional changes. This is due to differences in how USB devices are handled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:79
#: 7c7e2a529e1e4a1799b328d1576d5483
msgid "Using SITL with WSL and XWindows (Windows 10 only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:81
#: 1923f9abef2040cbbc8ad1b576b6cfa6
msgid "Windows 11 has a built-in XServer that is automatically set up. This section can be skipped if you are using Windows 11."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:83
#: f68af50a04ee49ba87328b2028b9b1a9
msgid "When using SITL (e.g. ``Tools/autotest/sim_vehicle.py``) with default options or ``--console --map`` an installed XWindows application must be started first. If not, the following error message will appear when running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:89
#: ac56d201bf734015b1af224f79f8a99e
msgid "Open the \"Ubuntu\" application and add the following to the end of ``~/.bashrc``. Be sure to comment and uncomment the appropriate lines depending on if you are using WSL1 or WSL2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:101
#: ffbd1236bb4b4350bc7a314e99aef06c
msgid "Using VcXsrv to Create XWindows Displays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:103
#: c9efd1476cc04530bf22edca7f985363
msgid "Select display settings: \"Multiple Windows\" but it is your preference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:104
#: 3f03eda6f0eb49f48a34ea5249da0bea
msgid "Select how to start clients: **Must** select **\"Start no Client\"**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:105
#: 54328b5f8b404633950ac8b33b7b2c93
msgid "Extra settings: **Must** check **\"Disable access control\"**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:109
#: 96460912a58d49f3bb51113db9b05698
msgid "If you have an issue with display check the following firewall rules,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:110
#: 6cae3202e83b4af382c453a702927062
msgid "Go to ``Windows Defender Firewall`` and click ``Advanced Settings`` (opens ``Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:111
#: a257af0dfc7541ccb49d8d78090251c0
msgid "Under ``Inbound Rules`` find ``VcXsrv windows xserver`` and ensure ``Allow Connection`` is enabled for your network type ``Private``, ``Public``, or both"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:112
#: 20d4d19e0ee14247a6986c726fec9005
msgid "Check ``Outbound Rules`` as well"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:114
#: eaed6b6c9d4a4af2950401f96ee0aa4e
msgid "this step is not required in Win11 since it already integrates the graphical interface into its WSL2 environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:118
#: af09ad32ee9c466d909d67d0f5ea49c6
msgid "Code Editing in WSL Using VSCode (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:120
#: eeb468d7b7124a8aad90bb7fc99c2499
msgid "VSCode can be installed on the Windows machine to edit and compile files inside of WSL. VSCode automatically integrates upon installation with WSL. More details are available :ref:`here<editing-the-code-with-vscode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:122
#: a41a5c3953d141e4ae910b5272291691
msgid "Do not install VSCode inside of WSL using, for example, apt-get."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:123
#: 8cf34ab5f5854d48bc9e12fa9c58d9d8
msgid "Be sure that the folder you are working on is opened within the WSL remote. This can be achieved by clicking the green button in the bottom left corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:127
#: 8b1947304b6842248a8ac5cf8ee3a56b
msgid "Windows Terminal (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:129
#: 0281ea548e594634bdd8512cda57c01e
msgid "Windows Terminal enables multiple tabs that can switch between many Linux terminals, PowerShell, and more. Directions to install Windows Terminal `are here <https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/terminal/get-started>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:131
#: 67dd9ec585494bc78b1b27c65c1cac2c
msgid "You can change the default terminal when opening Windows Terminal by going to \"Settings\" and moving the Ubuntu section to be first in the ``list`` section of the ``settings.json`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:132
#: 21b3267305184dbf83457c0cb6ba326b
msgid "The default starting directory can be changed by adding the ``startingDirectory`` line below to your preferred location by following the example below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:133
#: 4e6771a2aaac488682a009f0fe510dca
msgid "Note a similar code block to the one shown below will be automatically generated based upon the version and distribution of Linux installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:147
#: 6f506c37f6964ede9796a10ddd984535
msgid "Git Integration with Windows Credential Manager (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:149
#: c7835e82087042ff9da3751adde3d9c8
msgid "Git's Credential Manager can be connected to Window's Credential Manager tokens. This connection prevents re-authentication requests when accessing remote repositories such as GitHub after closing WSL or restarting Windows. The first time a Git operation requires credentials a dialog box will appear automatically to enter your credentials. See this `guide <https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/tutorials/wsl-git#git-credential-manager-setup>`_ for more information regarding GIT and WSL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:158
#: ad283840af18411283b4b15628068a36
msgid "File System Access between WSL and Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:160
#: eba492e3124b4cd7a4bc139f2fc6dc7e
msgid "From within WSL, the Windows drives are referenced in the /mnt directory. For example, to list documents within your (<username>) documents folder: ``ls /mnt/c/'Documents and Settings'/<username>/Documents`` or ``ls /mnt/c/Users/<username>/Documents``. You can also use the command ``explorer.exe .`` to open a Windows file explorer window in the current Linux directory. Take care that the editor being used on the Windows side does not change the line endings. Corruption of files is possible if care is not taken when crossing between file systems. In Windows 11, the Linux file manager 'nautilus' or Windows 'explorer.exe' can be invoked from the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:162
#: 0174f0010b2c420abe55f2e21d8c971b
msgid "From within Windows 10, the WSL distribution's files are located at (type in windows Explorer address bar): ``\\\\wsl$\\<distribution name>`` (e.g. ``\\\\wsl$\\Ubuntu-20.04``). Within Windows 11, the files are accessible under the Ubuntu directory in file explorer. Be careful modifying WSL text files in Windows editors since line endings are different in the two file systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows10_new.rst:166
#: 370fcfb1f7bc45a7ad422c695d350963
msgid "When trying to run your Ground Control Station software on WSL, if the application returns an error \"fuse: device not found, try 'modprobe fuse' first\" then it will be better to either use `MAVProxy <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-choosing-a-ground-station.html#mavproxy>`_ or `MissionPlanner <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-choosing-a-ground-station.html#mission-planner>`_ as your default ground control station because WSL does not support fuse (for more information check : https://github.com/Microsoft/WSL/issues/17 ). As of now, this error has been seen while using `QGroundControl <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-choosing-a-ground-station.html#qgroundcontrol>`_ on WSL running Ubuntu 16.04."
msgstr ""
